      "text": "To determine the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by 33, we need to find the smallest number in the range from 1000 to 9999 that is a multiple of 33. We can do this by dividing 1000 by 33 and rounding up to the nearest whole number, then multiplying that number by 33.\n\nFirst, we perform the division:\n\\[ 1000 \\div 33 \\approx 30.303 \\]\nSince we need a whole number, we round 30.303 up to the next whole number, which is 31. This means we multiply 33 by 31 to find the smallest four-digit multiple of 33:\n\\[ 33 \\times 31 = 1023 \\]\n\nTo verify, we check that 1023 is indeed a four-digit number and a multiple of 33:\n\\[ 1023 \\div 33 = 31 \\]\nSince 1023 divided by 33 gives an integer (31), it confirms that 1023 is a multiple of 33.\n\nTherefore, the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by 33 is \\(\\boxed{1023}\\).",
