    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by \\(33\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the smallest four-digit number**:\n   The smallest four-digit number is \\(1000\\).\n\n2. **Find the remainder when \\(1000\\) is divided by \\(33\\)**:\n   We perform the division \\(1000 \\div 33\\):\n   \\[\n   1000 \\div 33 \\approx 30.303\n   \\]\n   The integer part of the quotient is \\(30\\). Therefore, we multiply \\(30\\) by \\(33\\) to find the product:\n   \\[\n   30 \\times 33 = 990\n   \\]\n   Now, we find the remainder by subtracting \\(990\\) from \\(1000\\):\n   \\[\n   1000 - 990 = 10\n   \\]\n   So, \\(1000\\) leaves a remainder of \\(10\\) when divided by \\(33\\).\n\n3. **Determine the next multiple of \\(33\\)**:\n   Since the remainder is \\(10\\), we need to add enough to cover this remainder. The next multiple of \\(33\\) is obtained by:\n   \\[\n   990 + 33 = 1023\n   \\]\n\n4. **Verify the result**:\n   We check if \\(1023\\) is divisible by \\(33\\):\n   \\[\n   1023 \\div 33 = 31\n   \\]\n   Since \\(1023\\) divided by \\(33\\) gives an integer quotient of \\(31\\), \\(1023\\) is indeed divisible by \\(33\\).\n\nTherefore, the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by \\(33\\) is \\(\\boxed{1023}\\).",
